WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.090
You're signing up for a new app.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.230
The form asks for your age.

3
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.470
You're 14, but your
fingers slip and type 41.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.310
Green tick.

5
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.550
Accepted.

6
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.410
Curious, you try 150.

7
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.010
Red error.

8
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.910
Then you leave the box blank.

9
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.690
Red error again.

10
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.610
So why does the form
stop 150 and a blank box,

11
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.150
but wave a wrong age straight through?

12
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.890
In this mission, you'll learn how validation
checks that input follows rules before

13
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.590
the program uses it.

14
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.550
You'll meet a range check, which
tests that a number is between limits,

15
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.110
and a presence check, which
makes sure something was entered.

16
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.160
Your mission: explain why the form
accepted 41 when you meant 14.
